+# Proof outline and node crosswalk
+
+The proof is the explicit (m^3)-term construction for (n=m^2).
+
+1. `PU-01` extracts `n = m*m` from `IsSquare n` and reduces the root to the
+   square case.
+2. `PU-02` defines `gridTriple` and `gridSequence`.
+3. `PU-03`, `PU-04`, and `PU-05` prove two-coordinate growth according as the first
+   differing lexicographic digit is `k`, `j`, or `i`.
+4. `PU-06` combines those cases with the pairwise laws for nested flat maps.
+5. `PU-07` proves all coordinates are in `[1,m*m]`.
+6. `PU-08` computes the list length as `m^3`.
+7. `PU-09` proves that every admissible length is at most `n^2`, making the
+   natural supremum genuinely bounded.
+8. `PU-10` inserts the construction into the exact supremum set and applies
+   `le_csSup`.
+9. `PU-11` transports the checked source-shaped theorem to the canonical root.
+10. `PU-00` records the resulting root theorem `theorem_complete : Statement`.
+
+Every node has a unique reverse anchor in `full-study.md`; the structured
+forward and reverse ledgers are in `readability-review.json`.
